 "gossip": {
  "text": "Andy, the vibes have taken a hit. Brian Branch, the Lions safety, is out with an Achilles injury, and guard Ben Bartch was ruled out this morning too. Cornerback D.J. Reed is questionable with his ribs. Yesterday I called my pick of your Lions over Rob's Ravens shrewd because Carolina had no starting cornerbacks. Today Detroit is missing pieces of its own secondary. The bookies barely blinked and nudged the Lions from 3 to 3.5 points favourites in Carolina. I'm less relaxed. You're the underdog in all three of your bets, and this isn't the week that changes it.\n\nRob and Darren don't get to gloat for long. Baltimore's top pass rusher, Trey Hendrickson, had surgery on a broken finger and misses Tennessee. Ronnie Stanley is questionable with a toe and Zay Flowers with a hamstring. My hunch is that a finger mends faster than an Achilles, which is why the Ravens' side of the Andy bets still looks the healthier one. But that's a hunch, not a doctor's note.\n\nSteve, the stiff back I mentioned yesterday has turned into a ruling: Josh Simmons is out at Las Vegas. Darren, Kyle Dugger is out and Bryan Cook is questionable, so yesterday's rumour of a secondary is now a vacancy. Meanwhile Rob is the favourite in all three of his bets and is insufferable about it. That's how I'd read his silence, anyway.",
  "written": "2026-10-03T06:16:24-07:00",
  "based_on": 14
 }
}